161
00:17:56.940 --> 00:18:06.849
Stefan Starflinger: And there, we wanted to test non-finality, so we would let the nodes kind of miss proposals for a longer period of time.

162
00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:13.350
Stefan Starflinger: But we had, quite the challenge to even get finality with, DevNet 9.

163
00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:20.980
Stefan Starflinger: From the beginning, because, there was some miscommunication, on a kind of readiness.

164
00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:26.549
Stefan Starflinger: And a lot of the nodes, I think 30% of the network went offline pretty quickly.

165
00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:36.700
Stefan Starflinger: During the gloss fork, that was mainly Prism. We deployed the trunk branches, and they didn't have all of the latest changes there.

166
00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:50.090
Stefan Starflinger: So, they couldn't go through the fork transition, which took a lot of the network offline straight away. And so, Layer 2s also didn't, have time to test, the fork transition.

167
00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:54.520
Stefan Starflinger: Very well, because it wasn't, finalizing.

168
00:18:54.800 --> 00:19:05.790
Stefan Starflinger: Also, the watchtower was running, and because we were using trunk branches, nodes were updating quite regularly and quite often.

169
00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:10.149
Stefan Starflinger: And the second issue was that when restarting Lighthouse.

170
00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:19.579
Stefan Starflinger: There, were some, caching inefficiency, so the hash of the nodes, pretty much exploded.

171
00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:25.960
Stefan Starflinger: And they went, OOM quite a lot, which was also,

172
00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:35.529
Stefan Starflinger: attributable to the large validator size that we had, so I think we had 4 million Validator keys on the network.

173
00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:47.280
Stefan Starflinger: Which basically stretched the resources, that all the clients had, even though we increased the node size to have 32 gigabits of RAM.

174
00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:56.089
Stefan Starflinger: gigabyte of RAM, but still a lot of the nodes, went OAM from Lighthouse after restarting.

175
00:19:56.190 --> 00:20:09.129
